==Strategy==
Due to everything on the stage spawning on a timer, it can be cheesed if [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Maglev Cat]] hits the first Gory for double cash and [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] is released to take down the base along with [[Crazed Cow Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Lion Cats]] before H. Nah even comes out. If H. Nah spawns faster than the base falls, then try the alternate cheese, where you can use A. Bahamut to knockback H. Nah so far behind the enemy base that A. Bahamut can take down the base without being hurt by the present H. Nah. For 4 crown, you can use Starting Money up combos and [[Thief Cat (Rare Cat)|Thief Cat]] to kill the initial Squire Rels for double cash, then deploy A. Bahamut and use the same cheese method.

If one does not wish to try cheesing, then a [[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk Cat]] stack is recommended. As long as you can outlast the Brollows, then tank or outrange Camelle long enough to kill him, the stage should be manageable. Really, anything with good range like [[Gross Cat (Normal Cat)|Macho Leg Cat]], [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|Dragon Cat]], [[Figure Skating Cats (Super Rare Cat)|Drama Cats]], etc., are good for fighting the Brollows and H. Nah. You don't necessarily need to bring extremely long-ranged units like [[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Hacker Cat]] to kill the Camelle, as you can always use Awakened Bahamut or Maglev to take his health away all in big bursts. Beware though, as the Camelle is buffed by 500% and does 13,185 damage per hit.

